cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. No manuscript DOI exists yet -- do not cite one that hasn't been assigned."
title: "NeuroMesh: A Topology-Inspired Bottleneck Controller for Multimodal MRI Segmentation (Pilot Study)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-21
type: software
authors:
  - name: "NeuroMesh contributors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "<this-repo-url>"
abstract: >
  Pilot study (n=4 validation, n=4 test patients) of a bottleneck controller
  for BraTS multimodal segmentation, evaluated for robustness to missing MRI
  modalities. Reports that the intended dynamic topology-adaptation mechanism
  was not clearly observed empirically; a largely static learned bottleneck
  gate is a more defensible description of the trained model's behavior.
